# Control Plane / Lab Plane

The control plane contains identity, content, progress, business data, orchestration metadata and administrative systems.
The lab plane executes intentionally vulnerable workloads.

Mandatory invariants:

- Lab workloads cannot reach control-plane databases, caches, secrets or management interfaces.
- Lab workloads cannot reach runner management services.
- Lab workloads cannot communicate across user/session boundaries unless a scenario explicitly models shared networking.
- Public users do not connect directly to runner management addresses.
- Access to lab services is brokered through session-aware gateways.
- Public beta/production should place control and lab planes on separate hosts/VMs or equivalent strong boundaries.
